## Context

`plot_exp2_coverage_certainty.py` currently annotates individual GPT run
labels on the scatter and renders `no_report` runs (zero-coverage points)
as a distinct marker. Both clutter the figure for a conference audience.

Author decision (2026-05-25):
- Remove per-run GPT text labels from the scatter
- Remove `no_report` marker type entirely (exclude those runs from the plot)

Blocked by 0313 because the figure should be regenerated on clean data.

## Changes

In `src/aedist/plot_exp2_coverage_certainty.py`:
1. Remove the `ax.annotate(...)` calls that label individual GPT runs
2. In the data-loading loop, skip rows where `classification == "no_report"`
   (or equivalent zero-coverage sentinel) rather than plotting them at (0,0)

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No per-run text labels on the scatter
- [ ] `no_report` runs excluded from the figure (not plotted at zero)
- [ ] Figure regenerates cleanly after 0313 is merged
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
